c science space i would  say in terms of challenges in raising  money for the capstone campaign  right so ultimately whatever it was 30  million bucks the challenges  were on one hand specific to mdma  because of its history  of use as ecstasy in a recreational  context  a drug of potential abuse which many  people  don't realize was actually preceded by  its use therapeutically  under code name adam for quite some time  in the underground  there is that association that needed to  be overcome for some of the  organizations involved to ultimately  commit and be very very supportive  there were otherwise really only the  challenges that you face when raising  money for non-profits  and for non-profit causes especially  from business folks  a lot of them like to make money and  will either give you the line that you  know for-profit market-driven solutions  are going to be the best solution  although i think maps does a good job of  that  with their uh pharmaceutical development  co  and uh you know if they claim you know  one tip is if a billionaire tells you  that they have liquidity issues  that just means they don't want to do it  and you shouldn't waste your breath  trying to convince them otherwise move  on to the next person  so there you have it but ultimately it  was a lot easier than expected  curious about your thoughts on your own  kind of past upbringing maybe even your  trauma  how any of that is really connected to  the fact that you really [ __ ] more  towards being an individual performer  whether that's  wrestling or martial arts tango your  business  really kind of as a solopreneur that you  are really more comfortable as the  individual performer hey thanks for the  question yeah but i think for sure  it's possible that the  [Music]  uh upbringing being the oldest child uh  being also a runt when i was growing up  so  the sports that were available to me  were mostly individual it wasn't  necessarily byproduct of trauma just  really small so doing 