intment so when  something comes up we will ask when  would be a good time  to have a chat or may i make an  appointment  to chat about a few things that are on  my mind so then you have a set  point in time when you know you'll be  discussing these things  another tool in the toolkit is byron  katie's the work  there are certain exercises that you can  use as well as morning pages to kind of  defuse  or at least in some ways deconstruct  your own beliefs before you bring them  to your partner hey tim my question is  how do you figure out where to live  i'm thinking about moving to a new city  i was wondering if you have any  experience  or knowledge in figuring out which  factors carry the most  weight when looking to move somewhere  new a good place to start i think is  asking yourself  why do i want to leave where i am  currently rather than pick a full-time  destination you might look at how you  could test drive  a number of different locations for say  at least two weeks just enough to see  some variations in weather for instance  and  to give yourself a chance to explore and  get a feel for the personality of the  cities of course there are a lot of  popular places right now  tons of folks moving to florida tons of  folks moving  to say colorado to nashville  there's a long list the third coast  austin texas certainly is popular  and i feel like half of los angeles is  here already i would encourage you to  also look at  which factors that are compelling you to  move  are internal versus external so there  may be things  to work on that otherwise will follow  you to wherever your next destination is  hey tim franz here you talk a lot about  uh  hallucinogens uh psilocybe and and so  forth  and here in austria where i am it's very  hard to find  places or people who can do guided  sessions with yourself my wife  is working in the mobile palliative care  team here in salzburg and  i think they'd be really interested in  trying this out  uh at the end of of patients lives  and so i was just wondering what would  be your advice uh  how could i go about finding someone in  my area  since you're so connected in this field  uh i'd be very grateful  for your advice thanks man hey friends i  would have to know a lot more  about the specifics on the ground uh and  also i can't really give too much advice  certainly on this channel related to  something that might be  against the norms legally speaking where  you are but there are a few  things i might look into so i would  consider looking at  ketamine ketamine may be a legal option  at least it is in much of the united  states  where some of the other psychedelics are  not  and ketamine can be used in both  non-psychedelic and psychedelic doses  even though it's  known predominantly as an anesthetic hi  tim  my question is if there were one podcast  episode or one book of yours that you  would want your audience to share with  someone who has never heard of you  before  what would that be it depends on what  your objective is if you want to get  them hooked and  what their likes and dislikes are but i  would say a few that immediately come to  mind if you want to try to hook someone  would be jamie foxx the first episode i  did with him  elizabeth gilbert also extremely  extremely strong  or mary car both of those i think are  strong in some similar ways those would  be a few to start with hey tam this is  andrew from  colorado just wondering when we can  expect your next book  andrew as far as the next book goes i am  strongly contemplating putting together  a book on my healing  journey which certainly would include  many  of the excursions into non-ordinary  states of consciousness  which would include psychedelics it  would include  other let's just call it modalities as  well and one of the challenges  for me is determining how to write such  a book  about direct experiences some of which  seem to defy any  western rational scientific  explanation at least for the time bein